1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:01,940
Matthew 5

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:08,200
Seeing the crowds, he went up on the mountain, and when he sat down, his disciples came to him.

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,000
And he opened his mouth and taught them, saying,

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:16,400
Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.

5
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:21,160
Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.

6
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:25,000
Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,400
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they shall be satisfied.

8
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:36,220
Blessed are the merciful, for they shall receive mercy.

9
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:41,280
Blessed are the pure in heart, for they shall see God.

10
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:46,640
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called sons of God.

11
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,740
Blessed are those who are persecuted for righteousness' sake, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.

12
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,960
Blessed are you when others say,

13
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:54,980
Blessed are you when others say,

14
00:00:54,980 --> 00:01:00,540
Others revile you, and persecute you, and utter all kinds of evil against you falsely on my

15
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:07,760
account. Rejoice and be glad, for your reward is great in heaven. For so they persecuted the

16
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:14,840
prophets who were before you. You are the salt of the earth. But if salt has lost its taste,

17
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:21,960
how shall its saltiness be restored? It is no longer good for anything, except to be thrown

18
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:28,960
out and trampled under people's feet. You are the light of the world. A city set on a hill cannot

19
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:36,100
be hidden. Nor do people light a lamp and put it under a basket, but on a stand, and it gives light

20
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:43,060
to all in the house. In the same way, let your light shine before others, so that they may see

21
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:49,980
your good works, and give glory to your Father who is in heaven. Do not think that I have come

22
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,940
to abolish the law or the prophets.

23
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:59,040
I have not come to abolish them, but to fulfill them. For truly I say to you, until heaven and

24
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:05,100
earth pass away, not an iota, not a dot, will pass from the law until all is accomplished.

25
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:11,960
Therefore, whoever relaxes one of the least of these commandments, and teaches others to do the

26
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:17,440
same, will be called least in the kingdom of heaven. But whoever does them, and teaches them,

27
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:21,140
will be called great in the kingdom of heaven. For I tell you,

28
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:21,940
unless you are a man of God, you are not a man of God. You are not a man of God. You are not a man

29
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:27,080
of God. Your righteousness exceeds that of the scribes and Pharisees. You will never enter the

30
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:33,520
kingdom of heaven. You have heard that it was said to those of old, You shall not murder,

31
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:40,200
and whoever murders will be liable to judgment. But I say to you, that everyone who is angry

32
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,500
with his brother will be liable to judgment. Whoever insults his brother will be liable to

33
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:51,240
the council, and whoever says, You fool, will be liable to the hell of fire.

34
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:58,460
So, if you are offering your gift at the altar, and there remember that your brother has something

35
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:04,860
against you, leave your gift there before the altar, and go. First be reconciled to your brother,

36
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:10,260
and then come and offer your gift. Come to terms quickly with your accuser,

37
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:14,960
while you are going with him to court, lest your accuser hand you over to the judge,

38
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:21,600
and the judge to the guard, and you be put in prison. Truly I say to you, you will never get out,

39
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:21,920
until you are in prison. You will never get out until you are in prison. You will never get out,

40
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:27,060
until you have paid the last penny. You have heard that it was said,

41
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:32,500
You shall not commit adultery. But I say to you, that everyone who looks at a woman with

42
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:38,920
lustful intent has already committed adultery with her in his heart. If your right eye causes

43
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:44,640
you to sin, tear it out and throw it away. For it is better that you lose one of your members,

44
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:49,900
than that your whole body be thrown into hell. And if your right hand causes you to sin,

45
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,920
cut it off and throw it away.

46
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:57,360
For it is better that you lose one of your members, than that your whole body go into hell.

47
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:04,480
It was also said, Whoever divorces his wife, let him give her a certificate of divorce.

48
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:11,200
But I say to you, that everyone who divorces his wife, except on the ground of sexual immorality,

49
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:16,700
makes her commit adultery, and whoever marries a divorced woman commits adultery.

50
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,800
Again you have heard that it was said to those of old,

51
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,920
You shall not commit adultery.

52
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:26,040
You shall not swear falsely, but shall perform to the Lord what you have sworn.

53
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:32,380
But I say to you, do not take an oath at all, either by heaven, for it is the throne of God,

54
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:38,940
or by the earth, for it is his footstool, or by Jerusalem, for it is the city of the great king.

55
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:44,340
And do not take an oath by your head, for you cannot make one hair white or black.

56
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:50,700
Let what you say be simply yes or no. Anything more than this comes from evil.

57
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:56,880
You have heard that it was said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth.

58
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:03,040
But I say to you, do not resist the one who is evil, but if anyone slaps you on the right cheek,

59
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:07,820
turn to him the other also. And if anyone would sue you and take your tunic,

60
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,540
let him have your cloak as well. And if anyone forces you to go one mile,

61
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:16,760
go with him two miles. Give to the one who begs from you,

62
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,740
and do not refuse the one who would borrow from you.

63
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:25,980
You have heard that it was said, You shall love your neighbor and hate your enemy.

64
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:31,820
But I say to you, love your enemies, and pray for those who persecute you,

65
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:38,140
so that you may be sons of your Father who is in heaven. For he makes his sun rise on the evil

66
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:42,680
and on the good, and sends rain on the just and on the unjust.

67
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:49,720
For if you love those who love you, what reward do you have? Do not even the

68
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:53,500
tax collectors do the same? And if you greet only your brothers,

69
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:59,300
what more are you doing than others? Do not even the Gentiles do the same?

70
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:04,660
You, therefore, must be perfect, as your heavenly Father is perfect.

